      {
        "id": 2915650,
        "name": "Elathy Maricadie",
        "username": "Elathy_Maricadie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/elathy_maricadie/{size}/379496_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-08-19T22:22:18.290Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Alexia_Chamade\" data-display-name=\"Alexia Chamade\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"516686\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/alexia_chamade/48/508297_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Alexia Chamade:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It’s clear all accounts are controlled by the same player, but I can’t understand how one person could control dozens of accounts and cause such sustained damage?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Goonswam have created their own version of EVE-O or similar. Which makes it a breeze to cycle through Clients rapidly, this way it’s easy to get multiple clients on the same server tick.</p>\n<p>You cannot have one key, or combination of keys (ctrl, alt, and/or shift + key), press do multiple actions. This would be referred to as a macro (or sequence of key strokes).</p>",
