      {
        "id": 2915741,
        "name": "Meridan Night",
        "username": "Meridan_Night",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/meridan_night/{size}/488304_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-08-20T01:51:36.576Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Alexia_Chamade\" data-display-name=\"Alexia Chamade\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"516686\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/alexia_chamade/48/508297_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Alexia Chamade:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>and cause such sustained damage?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If you’re wondering why multiple characters did identical damage to you, it was because they had identical skills and fit and all got to fire a single round of missiles at you before you died. One of the Ospreys got two rounds in, and then you popped and the others didn’t apply. They only need to cycle F1 through the different accounts and the rest takes care of itself usually. Not saying they didn’t input broadcast, but the killmail doesn’t definitively prove it.</p>\n<p>I personally don’t see much fun in going out alone in your 10 accounts for some kills – seems a lot more trouble than it’s worth. Situational awarenes in EVE is complex enough without the added awareness of what your 10 accounts are doing at any given time.</p>",
